      },
      "message": "feat(post): Sodick wire EDM post, 2-axis contour from the 1998 operation manual\n\nassets/posts/sodick-wire.cps (\"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\") is the second\nwire post, never the default. It writes a vertical 2-axis Wire Contour in\nthe words of Sodick's \"Wire EDM Machine Operation\" manual (1998, Mark 21 /\nEX21): G20/G21, G90, G54-G59, G00, G40 G01, G02/G03 with incremental I J,\nT91/T90 for the wire, the condition id as a C word, M00/M01/M02. Taper,\n4-axis, a leaning or posed move, a rotary, a non-wire machine and a\ncondition id that is not C and three digits are refused by name. The\nprogram header says the words were not verified on a control.\n\nNot run on a Sodick control. Decision and the unconfirmed list:\ndocs/decisions/617-sodick-wire-post.md. Follow-ups: #1496-#1501.\n\nFixes #617\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
