      "message": "fix(post): Sodick wire cancels offset before positioning; name the condition table\n\nReview of PR #1506:\n- G40 now rides the section's first motion, the G00 to the threading\n  point, not the first cut: a wire offset left by an earlier program can\n  no longer shift the positioning or the threading point. The manual\n  shows G40 on a move (\"G40 Y-.02\"); RS-274 / ISO 6983 put G40 in its\n  own modal group, so it may share the block with G00, and a cancel with\n  no offset active is legal.\n- The header says every C condition named below must exist in the\n  control's condition table before start, and each section names its\n  own condition before its first motion.\n- The Sodick golden is regenerated; tests, the decision record and\n  assets/posts/AGENTS.md follow.\n\nRefs #617\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
